# SPH dam break. Mueller, Charypar & Gross (2003).
#
# SPH is meshless, so the boundary lines here only set the domain walls the particles are
# reflected off -- there is no border ring of cells and no pressure boundary condition.
# `region fluid` is what the solver seeds particles from, on a lattice of the configured
# spacing, and `region solid` is collided with ANALYTICALLY: the cylinder is a cylinder,
# not a staircase, because there is no mask to voxelise it onto.

sampling center

boundary xmin noslip
boundary xmax noslip
boundary ymin noslip
boundary ymax noslip

region fluid box min=(0.0,0.0,-1) max=(0.4,0.6,1)
region solid cylinder axis=z center=(0.7,0.15) radius=0.08
